<section class="why-accountability">
  <div class="site-container why-accountability__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Accountability</p>

      <h2>
        You should know who owns the outcome.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="why-accountability__content">
      <p>
        Complex work becomes risky when responsibility is spread so
        widely that nobody really owns the result. Our approach favours
        clear responsibility, visible decisions and practical escalation.
      </p>

      <div class="why-accountability__items">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Clear ownership</strong>
          <p>
            Responsibilities should be identifiable throughout delivery.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Visible decisions</strong>
          <p>
            Important technical or commercial decisions should not disappear
            into undocumented conversations.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Honest constraints</strong>
          <p>
            Risks and limitations should be surfaced early enough to be useful.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Practical handover</strong>
          <p>
            Clients should retain the information and access needed to operate
            what has been delivered.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

